# 1157 — Derive the next ordinary Room frontier from actual paid history

Date: 2026-10-04 · Status: implementation packet; independent review and whole-room acceptance open

## Decision and authority

The host needs to progress a confirmed ordinary Room beyond its first contact.
Decision1154 selects the confirmation contact only; decision1152 proves the
caller-selected paid operation; decision1153 refreshes existing companions.
None selects or creates the next reachable work station. Add one stateless
ordinary Room frontier helper over these actual owners. It owns no Site,
Project, goods, work, route, claim or permission ledger.

The construction lane owns only new `underground_room_frontier.gd` and its UID,
new `test_underground_room_frontier.gd` and its UID, this decision and dedicated
`underground-room-frontier-2026-10-04` evidence. Session/Settlement dispatch,
shared producers, registry and global census remain separately owned. The independently accepted1152 provider and actual first-cube diagnostic are
committed as2ac43b6c. This separate frontier packet grants no broader production
source, native, whole-room or runtime acceptance.

## Bounded selection packet

The approved public cold APIs split identity selection from contact observation:

- `next_site_into(actual_provider, room, after_key, original_cold, max_checks,
  out_candidate) -> StringName` copies one exact canonical Site/operation and
  current Project/pause/history/source facts. This output has no permission.
- `contact_into(actual_provider, candidate, access, approach_profile,
  approach_revision, original_cold, max_checks, out_request) -> StringName`
  rechecks that complete original tuple, then proves a unique already-published
  WORK endpoint through fresh WorkFace and both directed current paths.

Both outputs remain unchanged on refusal. The candidate and output request are
caller-owned synchronous packets under that exact cold token, not saved state.
The helper never mutates the phase provider's retained request or scratch.
Contact refuses any active Project instead of reopening it; selection still
reports its exact identity and pause state so the host can use ordinary resume
or settlement APIs. No caller box, success boolean or source permission is
accepted. The host must drop the query and both packets, release the cold lease,
and use normal phase admission; a stale candidate cannot cross leases.

The concrete provider's exact script and reciprocal current owner binding are
required. World/Nodes/Buildings observations remain in the existing WorkFace
seam. The final helper checks direct canonical Site/Project/Room fields, original
source and lease, full endpoint payloads and original caller candidate again.
No new generic observer interface or virtual final permission is introduced.

`after_key` is a bounded search position in the existing canonical Sites order,
not saved paid progress. It may skip a previously inspected inaccessible cube;
it cannot change that cube's state. Source or Room changes require a new scan.
The helper selects the next current Room-owned incomplete Site after that key,
then derives contact candidates from complete current WORK source rows and
already live full WORK endpoints. One invocation attempts one Site's unique
contact and at most one large WorkFace proof. The host may inspect another Site
after a refusal; no unbounded repeated full proof runs inside a single call.
An output Site/key identifies the inspected frontier only after current source
and full identity checks; a nonempty refusal never grants its contact.

BRACE/CUT/FINISH derive from canonical installed-support and physical-phase
columns, including paid work retained after cancellation. Completed
SUPPORTED_VOID is skipped. A currently active or paused Project is reported
without opening another phase or changing pause state. BACKFILL/closure is not
automatically selected. Full Room and Site identities are compared before and
after observations, and exact current paid cut history remains authoritative.

The complete actual WorkFace proves source body, held tool, stance, contact,
recovery and current Terrain. Separate explicit directed route certificates
prove access → work and work → retreat. The forward and backward source rows
may differ. No ground route, corner turn, endpoint, support or air is inferred
from coordinate adjacency. Legacy automatic WALK may correctly refuse until
the separately reviewed1156 source path is available.

## Publication boundary

Current ordinary phase preparation is refresh-only:
`Locations._refreshed_room_rows_refusal` requires identical live/staged presence
and payloads, so a new endpoint cannot be smuggled into the phase candidate.
Generic live Locations and WorldRoutes preparations have separate swaps and
fallible observations between them; sequentially publishing them is not an
atomic new-frontier transaction. The helper therefore selects only an already
published, fully proved contact. Missing contact/path returns the actual named
refusal and leaves every live bank unchanged.

The actual test finishes BRACE/CUT/FINISH, selects the next canonical Site,
and returns `ROOM_FRONTIER_EXISTING_CONTACT_REQUIRED` with unchanged request
and geometry. The existing producer boundaries remain unchanged and read-only:
`_refreshed_room_rows_refusal` returns `LOCATION_ROOM_REFRESH_ONLY` on changed
presence/payload, and `phase_prepared_leaf_refusal` returns
`LOCATION_PHASE_REFRESH_ONLY` on changed count/free count. A future publication
seam needs a concrete exact
Room/Site/section/source context, full completed support and body proof, both
directed path proofs, original cold/Space/Location/Route tokens, prepublication
observers followed by one pure final leaf, and one static bank-swap tail. This
packet does not invent that seam or broaden an existing phase context.

## Lifetime and work accounting before allocation

The module retains no member fields. Its caller candidate/request and one private query
exist only under the original cold lease and are destroyed before release;
the host may retain only copied scalar request IDs, which carry no permission.
No per-Room or per-Site array, dictionary, cached source image or second phase
context is allocated. Before allocation the current layout ceiling is one99-byte Candidate, one68-byte
Request output, one private Query holding a copied99-byte Candidate plus68-byte
Request,92 declared numeric bytes and one fixed I32[1] result. The emitted
private Query is263 bytes; caller packets are167 bytes. With the1024-byte helper
reservation and included512-byte reference/native allowance, the total is
1,966/2,048. Source-derived maximum own chain144 plus conservative existing
foreign512 and expression/result128 is784/1024. The reproducible census pins
all fields and allocation sites; this remains neither a new global reserve
nor an allocation measurement.

The2048-byte synchronous helper envelope is taken from the existing
1,048,960-byte cold operation, not from the last194 proposed global bytes.
It coexists with the existing WorkFace378,880-byte maximum; source-derived
combined peak is380,928/1,048,960. Its caller outputs are explicitly destroyed
before the separate phase peak1,048,912/1,048,960. This does
not increase a reservation or claim native qualification. No cold query runs
inside Structure CHECK's near-full lifetime. Site/contact enumeration spends
from one caller-bounded counter; one attempted WorkFace and the two route
queries retain their existing finite owner limits, with complete invocation
counts documented. Search timing and whole-tick acceptance remain open. Scan exhaustion is
`ROOM_FRONTIER_SCAN_END`, not Room completion; a test reaches it while all16
Kitchen claims remain unpaid.

## Required evidence

Use real Room claim ownership, actual Sites and source/geometry owners. Cover
canonical completed-cube skipping, canceled paid progress reuse, active/paused
preservation, foreign generation and source/lease changes, absent/ambiguous
contact, no-route refusal and original output/game state on failure. Actual
paid producer fixtures may be reused only with their synthetic source boundary
stated; they cannot qualify a production-success path. A real source-qualified
positive is separate and must not be manufactured by source flags, Site bytes,
pose teleportation or free geometry. Whole Kitchen remains open until the host
can complete every required cube with real motion and publication.

Sources: settlement_rules_v2; movement amendment SET-MOVE-001; the underground
economic amendment; decisions1152–1154 and1156; current actual Sites,
WorkFace, Locations and WorldRoutes implementations; parent lease authorization.
